{# PRESENCE — "this area has no zones yet".

   An org that has never imported a zoning scheme must not meet a half-drawn zone dashboard: it
   meets ONE plate that says what a zone is and offers the one way to make some. Nothing else on
   the surface renders, and no zone furniture appears anywhere else in the product — no zone
   column, no zone filter, no zone map layer — until the first import lands.

   Rendered by ZonesController when ZoneRepository::zonesFor($area) is empty. #}
<div class="c zempty">
    <span class="zeh">This area has no zones yet</span>
    <p class="zeb">A zone is <b>a lens, not a fence</b>: it gives every module a second way to group what it
        already shows — “patrols by zone”, “incidents by zone” — and never hides or blocks a record.
        Import a GeoJSON FeatureCollection, one named polygon per zone, and the whole set lands at once.</p>
    <p class="zeb">Until then {{ area.name }} simply has none: no zone column, no zone filter, no zone map layer
        anywhere in the product.</p>

    <div class="zea">
        {{ include('zones/_draw_soon.html.twig') }}
        {% if canManage %}
            {# The same all-or-nothing import the panel offers, in the one place there is nothing
               else to offer. A reader sees the copy and no form: importing is Manager-and-up. #}
            <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_area_zones_import', {uuid: area.uuid}) }}"
                  enctype="multipart/form-data" data-zone-import class="zea-form">
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('zone_manage') }}">
                <input type="file" name="zones" accept=".geojson,.json,application/geo+json,application/json"
                       class="fld" aria-label="Zones GeoJSON file" required>
                <button class="cta" type="submit">{{ ux_icon('lucide:upload') }}Import GeoJSON</button>
            </form>
        {% endif %}
    </div>

    <p class="zeb"><span class="mono d" style="font-size:10.5px">or from a terminal: app:zone:import {{ area.uuid }} zones.geojson</span></p>
</div>
